 ### Reference Standards
 **All citations must be real, no mocking**—must verify via search, fabricating any author, title, year, or page number is prohibited.
 
+For Markdown-first research reports, source markers such as `[^123^]` map by exact numeric `id` to the citation JSONL supplied with the Markdown, or to `/mnt/agents/.store/citation.jsonl` when no file is supplied. Treat the Markdown as canonical content and the HTML as a presentation-only projection. Use the matched metadata to build whatever citation treatment fits the PDF. References are optional rather than mandatory for this handoff. If an ID cannot be resolved, preserve the marker and report it instead of inventing or dropping a source.
+
 #### Strict Correspondence Constraint
 In-text `<a href="#ref-1">[1]</a>` must strictly correspond to end-of-document `<li id="ref-1">`:
 - `id` must be unique and matching
